    STEP A-3.16: Bootstrap Allocator Correctness Closure
    
    Four P0 closures per Steward STEP A-3.16 mandate:
    
    C1: REGISTRY PROTOCOL — slot acquisition now uses three-phase protocol:
        RESERVE (CAS ptr 0 → RESERVE_SENTINEL) → INIT (write size) → PUBLISH
        (CAS RESERVE_SENTINEL → actual ptr with release). Readers use
        acquire-load and skip 0/sentinel slots. Deregister CASes actual → 0
        with release ordering. Prevents ABA: a reader observing ptr=P cannot
        read stale metadata after slot reuse (reuser must pass through
        RESERVE_SENTINEL first).
    
    C2: REALLOC FAILURE SAFETY — old pointer's registry entry is NOT
        deregistered until new allocation succeeds AND data is copied. If
        real_malloc fails, returns NULL and leaves old ptr valid per POSIX.
        Both pre-init and post-init bootstrap realloc paths fixed.
    
    C3: POINTER CLASSIFICATION — is_bootstrap_ptr() now does EXACT-MATCH
        against registry instead of range-based address comparison. Unknown
        pointers in buffer range are NOT treated as bootstrap; they fall
        through to real allocator with a diagnostic counter
        (g_bootstrap_unknown_in_range). Eliminates silent memory-leak risk.
    
    C4: REGISTRY EXHAUSTION — when registry is full, bootstrap_alloc()
        returns NULL (hard-fail) instead of returning an untracked
        allocation. Diagnostic counter (g_bootstrap_registry_full) records
        the event. Callers (dlsym) must handle NULL gracefully.
    
    Tests (scripts/ci/test_profiler_v6.c): 62 tests, 0 failures.
      T1: basic correctness (9 tests)
      T2: bootstrap handoff with exact-match classification (16 tests)
      T3: min copy semantics (3 tests)
      T4: multithreaded normal path (9 tests)
      T5: overflow guards (5 tests)
      T6: registry exhaustion — fill 64 slots, verify 65th fails (6 tests)
      T7: failure injection — force real_malloc NULL, verify ptr survives (8 tests)
      T8: concurrency + ABA + slot reuse (6 tests, 4 threads x 100 iters)
    
    TSan: 0 data races detected (T1-T8 under TSan with halt_on_error=0).
      T5 (malloc SIZE_MAX) causes TSan allocation-size-too-big abort, a
      TSan limitation not a profiler defect.
    
    ASan: SKIPPED — ASan interposes malloc, conflicting with the profiler's
      LD_PRELOAD interposition. Fundamental limitation of combining two
      malloc interposers. Test harness memory safety verified by plain run.
    
    Node.js v24 smoke test under PROD variant: exit 0, no crash.
    
    No push (awaiting Steward approval). No changes to workflow Base64 blob.
